# Recordings from the guided runs: eye positions, eye distance and
# pupil diameters, frame by frame -- biometric data of a real person.
# Kept on a private branch, off every public remote.
# Anchored to the root on purpose: the kept copies live under
# a private branch and have to stay trackable there.
/field-scan-samples.csv
/tilt-scan-samples.csv
/sweep-samples.csv

# Neural-network weights from third parties are never committed. What a
# set of weights was trained on is a separate question from what this
# code may do, and for the opentrack head-pose models that question has an
# uncomfortable answer: their training data carries non-commercial terms.
#
# openstargazer's own weights, trained on replicantface (MIT) from scratch,
# are GPL-3.0 and live under openstargazer/models/. They are the exception.
*.onnx
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
!openstargazer/models/head-pose.onnx

# Camera frames are photographs of whoever is sitting in front of the
# tracker, in their room. Same rule as the recordings above, one step
# more sensitive: they belong on a private branch and
# nowhere near a branch that goes public.
/camera-frame.*
/*.pgm
/*.raw
